        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "The docs (`runtime/doc/syntax.txt`, `ft-markdown-syntax`) still document `g:markdown_fenced_languages` as working, but since #37907 the markdown ftplugin starts treesitter unconditionally. `vim.treesitter.start()` sets `b:ts_highlight`, which makes the `syntaxset` autocmd (`syntax/syntax.vim`) skip `set syntax=markdown` — `runtime/syntax/markdown.vim` never loads, so the variable is never read. The doc text is Vim-maintained and synced into Nvim; the behavior is Nvim's own, so the mismatch sits on the vim/nvim seam. Sibling regression from the same commit: #39433 (spell `[s`), fixed in `decoration.c`.",
