            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Measured on nvim 0.12.4 (default config, headless): ```c``` fence parses and yields 42 highlight captures (bundled `c.so` + `queries/c/highlights.scm`), while ```python```/```py```/```csv``` fences parse to nothing — no `python.so`/`csv.so` exists (`lib/nvim/parser/` ships only c, lua, markdown, markdown_inline, query, vim, vimdoc) and `vim.treesitter.language.add('python')` returns nil. The failure is silent: `get_parser` returns a lazy tree that fails at parse time, so `def`/keywords are simply dark.",
